    - target: {fileID: 5905881967701677635, guid: 3938ed1ae5c23814f8817ead1ed0d3bf, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: 'This scene demonstrates using event branches to react to various events.
        Event branches can trigger when an interrupt (such as a conditional abort)
        occurs, when a physics callback occurs, when an event occurs, etc. The behavior
        tree Start branch must be active in order for other event branches to be
        triggered.

        In this scene event branches are used to cause the character
        to jump, crouch, add the coin amount, and the end point. See this page for
        more details on creating your own event task:

        https://opsive.com/support/documentation/behavior-designer-pro/new-tasks/event-node/

'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7722742870279193141, guid: 3938ed1ae5c23814f8817ead1ed0d3bf, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: DescriptionPanel
